<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:50%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:180%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:180%;">Comparison with baseline methods and results in various datasets. <math id="S4.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math> indicates datasets with “step pseudo-label” from our pipeline, and “Exo.” denotes EgEx’s Exo view. “GT proposal” refers to experiments using ground truth action proposals as VLM input, without class information. Zero-shot VLM inference achieves around 30% accuracy in matching ground truth labels. InternVL2-40B-AWQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> is used as the frozen VLM. Following the original implementation, YT-Temporal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> pretrained Vid2Seq <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite> weights are used for initialization of SDVC, and fine-tuned using EgoGS annotations, with separate training for each hierarchy. We used the default configuration on SDVC.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
